summary:
  A second face is built when a seat asks for one that already lives.

history:
  Two faces are two search fields, two sets of station probes and two key
  handlers on one player. Built again on each move, the face started the
  list from the top, closed an open menu and asked the directory
  everything once more: 80 requests and 114 log errors over ten round
  trips, against none for the one face that is moved.

target:
  package/contents/ui/PlayerWindow.qml

find:
          if (!faceItem && face) faceItem = face.createObject(seatItem);

replace:
          if (face) faceItem = face.createObject(seatItem);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_playerwindow.qml::test_the_face_outlives_a_popup_seat_and_sits_in_the_next_one.
